        "title": "Graceful Pasupathinath",
        "text": "The temple is NOT crowded like our Indian temples and is kept very clean. The Western Face of Lord Pasupathinath is available for Darshan when the temple is open and  four faces (out of five)can be during the arthi in the morning and evening, when all four doors around the Lord are opened and we are permitted go round the Lord. The atmosphere at that time is mesmerizing! The staff near the gates speak very softly to the visitors!\nBehind the main temple, river Bhagmati can be seen and burning of bodies similar to that at Benares can be seen.\nWhat I did not like was the prohibition of photography, even around the temple.",
